---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { checkedOn, disclaimer } from "../content";
---
<Layout
  title="About this site"
  description="Who publishes musical.today, how its listings are checked, and why unannounced dates and venues are left blank rather than filled in."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>About this site</h1>
    <p class="lede">{disclaimer}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="container prose">
    <h2>How a listing gets here</h2>
    <p>
      A show appears when it is on sale through a seller that can be named,
      and the entry carries only what that seller's listing states. Dates,
      venue, price bands and cast are left blank until they are published —
      marked "to be announced" rather than filled in with the most plausible
      answer. Listings were last read on {checkedOn}.
    </p>
    <h2>Links out</h2>
    <p>
      The only outbound links are to ticket sellers, and they go through a
      redirect that is closed to search engines. This site earns nothing from
      them; it is a listings site, not a reseller, and it takes no booking and
      handles no payment.
    </p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If something here is wrong — a date that moved, a run that was cancelled,
      a show that never existed — it should be corrected rather than argued
      with. This page will carry a contact route once the site is past its
      first draft.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose p { max-width: 68ch; }
</style>
